.TH sleak 1  "sleak 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
sleak \- Sleak — the anti\-monolith architecture engine of ELCI. Detects, quantifies and explains where architectural responsibility concentrates in a Rust workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsleak\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sleak — the anti\-monolith architecture engine of ELCI. Detects, quantifies and explains where architectural responsibility concentrates in a Rust workspace
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Output format for scan/check/explain/diff: human or json. `scan`/`check` also accept sarif
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sleak\-scan(1)
Analyse the workspace and report findings. Always exits 0 on a successful run, regardless of what it finds
.TP
sleak\-check(1)
Analyse the workspace and fail (exit 1) if any finding is MAJOR or CRITICAL. The canonical CI invocation
.TP
sleak\-explain(1)
Explain one finding id: a general description of what it means, plus every currently\-detected finding with that id and its full evidence
.TP
sleak\-graph(1)
Export the raw architecture graph (nodes + edges), bypassing policy findings entirely
.TP
sleak\-baseline(1)
Manage the accepted\-debt baseline (directive §16)
.TP
sleak\-diff(1)
Compare the working tree\*(Aqs architecture against `git_ref` (directive §17) — did this change increase concentration? Informational: always exits 0 on a successful run, regardless of what it finds. Requires `path` to be a git repository
.TP
sleak\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
